{"name":"Sour Grapes","hex":"#785ca0","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sour grapes","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see sour,‎ grapes.","Things that somebody pretends to despise because they cannot obtain or have them."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour_grapes"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Fox and the Grapes","blocks":[{"text":"The Fox and the Grapes is one of Aesop's Fables, numbered 15 in the Perry Index. The narration is concise and subsequent retellings have often been equally so. The story concerns a fox that tries to eat grapes from a vine but cannot reach them. Rather than admit defeat, he states they are undesirable. The expression \"sour grapes\" originated from this fable. It was also adapted by La Fontaine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Chauveau_-_Fables_de_La_Fontaine_-_03-11.png/330px-Chauveau_-_Fables_de_La_Fontaine_-_03-11.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fox_and_the_Grapes","wikidata":"Q1193645"},{"title":"Sour Grapes (1998 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sour Grapes is a 1998 American black comedy film written and directed by Larry David and starring Steven Weber, Craig Bierko, Viola Harris, Karen Sillas, Robyn Peterman and Matt Keeslar. It was released on April 17, 1998, by Columbia Pictures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fb/Sour_Grapes_1998_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sour_Grapes_(1998_film)","wikidata":"Q1677306"},{"title":"Sourness","blocks":[{"text":"Sourness, also known as sour, is a basic taste sensation perceived through hydrogen ions from acidic compounds interacting with taste bud receptors, and it can also refer to an unpleasant or acidic quality in taste, disposition, or tone. It is a warning sign for potentially spoiled food, though it is balanced in some food products by sweetness, and it is associated with a low pH."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lemon_with_white_background.jpg/330px-Lemon_with_white_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourness","wikidata":"Q2795949"},{"title":"Grape","blocks":[{"text":"A grape is a fruit, botanically a berry, of the deciduous woody vines of the flowering plant genus Vitis. Grapes are a non-climacteric type of fruit, generally occurring in clusters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grape","wikidata":"Q10978"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Chauveau_-_Fables_de_La_Fontaine_-_03-11.png/500px-Chauveau_-_Fables_de_La_Fontaine_-_03-11.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Chauveau_-_Fables_de_La_Fontaine_-_03-11.png/1280px-Chauveau_-_Fables_de_La_Fontaine_-_03-11.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Chauveau_-_Fables_de_La_Fontaine_-_03-11.png/500px-Chauveau_-_Fables_de_La_Fontaine_-_03-11.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The illustration of the fable by François Chauveau in the first volume of La Fontaine's fables, 1668 ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChauveau_-_Fables_de_La_Fontaine_-_03-11.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/La_Fontaine_Louvre.jpg/500px-La_Fontaine_Louvre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail